question/problem "Given the vector $u$ has magnitude $4$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $9,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${75}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **one decimal place** where appropriate.\n\n$u\\times v≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{75}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =36\\cdot (0.965\\,92…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(34.773\\,32…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈34.8n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a166115-1a93-5945-bfac-b1d3ddb1cfbd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e51841e2-2012-549b-989a-37fd008f5468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e51841e2-2012-549b-989a-37fd008f5468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268158} :answer-field/id #uuid "050f56cb-5123-562f-bf7b-5b64589486fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268157}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12af4ca0-8959-5c7c-b7aa-9f46b71b36a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-278851" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $8$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $6$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${150}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n.$  \n\n$a\\times b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =8\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =24n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a166115-1a93-5945-bfac-b1d3ddb1cfbd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3705c4d-3406-5a73-b9a5-97585dcfa310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268161} {:answer/id #uuid "78a709f1-191c-5778-8666-3ac4d76c7db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78a709f1-191c-5778-8666-3ac4d76c7db1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268162} :answer-field/id #uuid "ece73327-ec62-50c9-a0e4-c944a0f3cbc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268160}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afbb8382-0b70-5287-99f8-b2adf01d136f" :question/math-academy-id "q-279275" :question/problem "The vector $a$ has magnitude $15$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $2$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${90}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n.$  \n\n$a\\times b=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =15\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{90}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =30\\cdot 1\\cdot n \\\\  & =30n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09aeb7f5-31e0-5b2d-9e2a-8eace54a6665" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cf6fa1c-dced-5860-8a4b-77a37f5d34a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30.15n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf6fa1c-dced-5860-8a4b-77a37f5d34a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30.15n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268165} :answer-field/id #uuid "b73c8626-a41c-5107-b9d1-2153b26b1cfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268164}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "824628c7-1546-5ed3-9b1a-834e6b63983a" :question/math-academy-id "q-279284" :question/problem "Given the vector $a$ has magnitude $11$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $3,$ the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${66}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **two decimal places** where appropriate.\n\n$a\\times b≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =11\\cdot 3\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{66}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =33\\cdot (0.913\\,54…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(30.146\\,82…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈30.15n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
